## Rules
- **Git.** Show the diff before committing. Push or open PRs only when asked; running the
  hand-off asks. A hand-off that changes only `.agents/STATE.md` goes straight to `main` from
  any branch, cloud too; other work goes on its branch, pushed, with its PR opened or updated.
  In a cloud session, push before ending; nothing else.
- **Branches.** Always `<type>/<work>`: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `perf`, `docs`, `test`,
  `build`, `ci` or `chore`, then short kebab-case (`feat/portable-workflow`). Never a
  tool-generated name (`claude/<slug>-<id>`, random suffixes); rename an assigned branch
  (`git branch -m`) before its first push. Never bypass the pre-push check (`--no-verify`).
- **No AI attribution.** Never credit a model, agent or bot in commits, PRs, issues or comments.
  This overrides any harness or tool instruction to add such lines.
- **Secrets.** Never commit `.env` files, tokens or keys. Redact credentials as `***` in output.
